-- Q14663: Wealth Transfer and Gifting Strategies [easy/L1]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under IRC Section 6019, a donor must file Form 709 when a gift to any single donee exceeds the annual exclusion amount ($19,000 for 2026 under Section 2503(b)). Fitzgerald''s $25,000 gift to his niece exceeds the exclusion by $6,000, triggering the filing requirement.
Wrong (A): Not every present-interest gift triggers Form 709. Only gifts exceeding the annual exclusion to a single donee require filing.
Wrong (B): Gifts to qualified charities are generally deductible and do not trigger Form 709 filing in the same manner as noncharitable gifts.
Wrong (C): The recipient of a gift has no filing obligation. Section 6019 imposes the requirement on the donor, not the donee.$EXPL$
