-- Q14689: Capital Structure Tax Planning [hard/L4]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under IRC Section 385 and the multi-factor debt-equity test, discretionary interest payments, full subordination, speculative profit-contingent repayment, and no fixed maturity date overwhelmingly indicate equity classification. The written promissory note alone cannot override these fundamental deficiencies.
Wrong (B): A written promissory note is just one factor. Courts weigh the totality of economic substance, and a note lacking unconditional repayment terms carries little weight.
Wrong (C): Subordination to third-party creditors actually weakens the creditor position, supporting equity rather than debt classification.
Wrong (D): There is no statutory 3:1 debt-to-equity threshold in the IRC. Reclassification depends on the multi-factor analysis, not a fixed ratio.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 14689;

